    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "documentation",
      "content": "## Technical Notes\n\n**System Pressure:** Low pressure steam at 100 kN/m² (1 bar) or 15 psi\n\n**Latent Heat:** 2201 kJ/kg (945 Btu/lb) for saturated steam\n\n### Key Principles\n\n- **Purpose:** Safety valves prevent system pressure from exceeding certification pressure\n- **Sizing Criterion:** Valve capacity must equal or exceed maximum boiler vapor output at working pressure\n- **Higher Pressure:** Compressed steam requires smaller valve (less volume)\n- **Lower Pressure:** Expanded steam requires larger valve (more volume)\n\n### Important Notes\n\n- Always consult manufacturer documentation before final design\n- This table is specifically for low pressure steam systems\n- For high pressure steam, different sizing applies\n- Proper valve selection is critical for system safety, especially with high-temperature steam and significant latent heat energy"
